      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T19:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "can we avoid allocating it on stack and generate directly inside kh_buf.vkh?\nstack size is an important limitation for cr50.\n\nand maybe it\u0027s time to just split u2f_generate into u2f_generate_v0 and u2f_generate_v1 based on kh_version at this point, rather than having multiple if-branches below",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 136,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "95e93bbf_3150475d",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 136,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-28T01:20:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t generate directly in kh_buf.vkh because the layout is:\n\nversion -- 1 byte\norigin_seed -- 32 bytes\nkh_hmac -- 32 bytes\nauthorization_seed -- 32 bytes ---\u003e needs to be word-aligned for TRNG to work\nauthorization_hmac -- 32 bytes\n\nHowever I can reuse the od_seed array because the authorization_seed is not used in kh_hmac derivation.",
      "parentUuid": "ac2ed8da_bc3916f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 136,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 136,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2e96588d_6231f8ae",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T19:32:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "does it mean the keyhandle doesn\u0027t include the auth_seed?\nkey_handle_size is 1*2*32, covers only the first 3 fields",
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c00dd4d9_2f54a99a",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T19:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the current implementation, yes, only the first 3 fields are used in computing kh_hmac. We could also move the auth_seed and auth_hmac to right after origin_seed, and use everything to compute the kh_hmac; this would solve the other problem you mentioned - we wouldn\u0027t need a U2F_VKH_KEYPAIR_INPUT_LEN or a header struct. It just feels a little strange to use one hmac as the input of another hmac - I don\u0027t know",
      "parentUuid": "2e96588d_6231f8ae",
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04917941_189c42ed",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-24T19:40:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I mean \u0027only the first 3 fields are used in computing the keypair\u0027.",
      "parentUuid": "c00dd4d9_2f54a99a",
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16ca065b_f07dc405",
        "filename": "common/u2f.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1345639
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-28T01:20:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"hmac inside hmac\" approach doesn\u0027t make much sense because the authorization_hmac will be public, and it doesn\u0027t buy anything to encode it into kh_hmac just for formatting.\n\nI\u0027m calling the first 3 fields (version, origin_seed, kh_hmac) \"struct u2f_versioned_key_handle_header\" like you suggested.",
      "parentUuid": "04917941_189c42ed",
      "revId": "3b8726cd482c0bc63c573862d4812a9f9519afb8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
