      "writtenOn": "2020-07-25T00:56:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As mentioned in common/u2f.c, I could do:\n\nstruct u2f_versioned_key_handle {\n        uint8_t version;\n        uint8_t origin_seed[U2F_P256_SIZE];\n        uint8_t authorization_seed[U2F_P256_SIZE];\n        uint8_t authorization_hmac[U2F_P256_SIZE];\n        /* HMAC of everything before */\n        uint8_t kh_hmac[U2F_P256_SIZE];\n};\n\nThen we don\u0027t need U2F_VKH_KEYPAIR_INPUT_LEN or a header substruct. I guess it\u0027s okay to input one hmac into another hmac?",
      "parentUuid": "608f6ae0_fe601f38",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 33
      },
